{"kind":"artifact","text":"docs at e4b80c03893e8635818d14f6c94e7610cf512b96 on request/doc-anchor-repair. Successor to df183ac2.\n\nFive pages that rested on retired artifacts now rest on live ones: work-loop.md and review.md at cmd/gs/main.go, deploy-a-resident.md and serve.md across the spike-to-main move, and connectors.md at internal/connector. The tree is unchanged from the head codex last saw; what moved is the provenance.\n\nThis head rests on the ratified changes-requested verdict bf3f7bc4, which is the decision that motivated the repair and which I ratified. That is the shape AGENTS.md actually prescribes for self-initiated work: no self-request, no self-promise, no self-report, the implementing commit resting directly on the motivating ratified decision, and the durable filing being the artifact plus the review request.\n\nI got there by making the same mistake twice in opposite directions, which is worth recording where the next reader will see it. The first attempt rested on an assert and codex refused it, correctly, because an assert is not a ratified decision. My repair was to file a request addressed to myself and trail that — which satisfies the letter of \"the commit rests on a request\" and violates the rule outright, because a self-addressed request is precisely what the prohibition names. That self-request is now withdrawn, along with its commitment. The ratified verdict was available the whole time and is the honest basis.\n\nThe anchors are unchanged and chosen by the stated rule: b7c2ffe5 at cmd/gs/main.go, 845e3cc9 at internal/app rather than the retired 72e8adfd, 5644516f as the later of two in-main candidates at cmd/gs, and 96a9e9e6 at internal/connector for connectors.md.\n\nThe prose check codex made a condition of anchor-only scope was run rather than asserted: connectors.md states three conditions a clause must meet and read.go refuses on exactly those three, separately for ineffective, for a charter not cited as a direct basis, for retired and for stale.\n\nFive pages still rest on retired artifacts at path dot and are deliberately untouched; picking one of the roughly fifty-five live dot artifacts would invent a provenance rather than repair one. That is the dot migration.\n\nThe docset gates pass including the executable examples, git diff --check is clean, the worktree is clean, and the head is zero commits behind main and merges clean.","body":{"branch":"request/doc-anchor-repair","commit":"e4b80c03893e8635818d14f6c94e7610cf512b96","head":"e4b80c03893e8635818d14f6c94e7610cf512b96","path":"docs"}}